course: dictionary
lesson: 801
title: Small word, many jobs
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word before is small, but it does many jobs. It can tell you about time, about place, or about order. The words around it show which job it is doing. «Before lunch, Jake had 15 marbles.» Here before means earlier than lunch.
explain: «She stood before the class.» Here before means in front of. Ask yourself what the sentence is about: time, place or order? A teacher standing before a class is standing in front of it, not earlier than it.
explain: Always check by swapping in your meaning. «Look before you cross» means look earlier than you cross, so looking comes first. If your meaning makes the sentence sensible, you have understood it.
fact: Before means earlier than something else, as in «before lunch».
fact: Before can mean at an earlier time, in the past, as in «I have been here before».
fact: Before can mean in front of, as in «the number before 10 is 9».
fact: «Before long» means soon, and «before you know it» means very soon.
fact: Formal writing often swaps before for words like «prior to», «previously» or «in advance of».
exercise: Jake had 15 marbles «before lunch». What does before mean here? | In front of lunch | Instead of lunch | *Earlier than lunch | Soon after lunch
exercise: «She stood before the class.» What does before mean here? | Far away from the class | After the class | Earlier than the class | *In front of the class
exercise: «Look before you cross.» Which thing should you do first? | Shout | *Look | Cross | Run
test: «I have been here before.» What does before mean? | *At an earlier time, in the past | In front of something | Very soon | Earlier than something else
test: Which number comes before 10? | 11 | *9 | 12 | 8
exam: Which word is a formal way to say before? | *Prior to | After | Later | Next
